"""Row data for the binding-rule classification.

One dict per binding sentence across the nine reference files under
skills/reckon-build/references. Key meaning:

    f  file, relative to skills/reckon-build/references
    l  line of the sentence's first line in that file
    r  the rule, quoted or tightly paraphrased
    e  the code that enforces it, as file:symbol, or "-" where none could be named
    t  a test that drives the guarded action far enough to fire the check, or "-"
    w  whether the rule is still wanted (this node's proposal; the lead confirms)
    d  disposition: keep, or delete-as-obsolete
    y  one line saying why

Read at the revision named in the fragment. Every file, symbol and test in a row
was resolved against the tree rather than recalled, and every cited test was run
in the foreground at that revision; a row whose guard no test shows firing is
not marked enforced and its reason says so.
"""

